  "truthReference": "Independent hand audit of validation/m12/fixtures/objective-c/*.{h,m} against Objective-C semantics and the M11 Objective-C contract (validated 1.000/1.000 in M11.10; symbols only). Symbols: @protocol -> interface with methods -> method; @interface class -> class with properties -> property and methods -> method (+ class methods via the + token, both method kind); @interface Class (Category) -> extension (category, symbol name = class name, never the category label); @implementation -> class with ivars -> property; methods -> method; C functions -> function; file-scope static vars -> variable. Noise: function-local variables (no symbol), blocks (no symbol), typedefs/enums/constants in .h config headers (parsed by the shared C-family path, same as C++ shape_config.h precedent). Relationships (family contract, matches Java M12.01 and C M12.16): contains = REAL container ownership only (class/protocol/extension -> member, interface -> method) — never `global contains X`; extends = class -> superclass, protocol -> adopted protocol; implements = class -> adopted protocol; calls = message expressions (source = enclosing method, target = SELECTOR — the first identifier after the receiver, never the receiver: [NSString stringWithFormat:] -> stringWithFormat not NSString; [super init] -> init not super; [message uppercaseString] -> uppercaseString not message) and C function calls; instantiates = [[Foo alloc] init] / [Foo new] (target = the class receiver); references = import/include dependencies (root -> module). Relationship sources are the enclosing METHOD name; top-level file-scope relationships use root. The config header user_config.h has no class-declaration markers so the shared C-family detection path parses it (constants -> constant, enum -> enum with members, typedef -> type, static var -> variable, function prototype -> function, contains for enum members) — identical to the C++ shape_config.h precedent; the differential encodes exactly what the pipeline emits. The modern `typedef NS_ENUM(...)` macro form is a genuine grammar gap (ERROR node) documented in docs/analyzers/real-objective-c-analyzer.md.",
